5	   "where": "Acceptance Criteria, LS-21 persisted-field AC (L1258, Method A) against LS-1 (L74) as amended",
6	   "issue": "Method A still says the test enumerates every member of `GraphState` and passes a member that is on the DERIVED allowlist. The amended LS-1, the writer-lint AC and ADR-0011 sections 6.1 and 6.3 say the opposite. `GraphState` now holds persisted columns only. The DERIVED allowlist is the member list of `GraphCaches`, `GraphScratch` and `GraphDiag`. An implementer following the AC would allow derived members inside `GraphState`, and the reflection test would not check the split that TR-lsg-038 exists to enforce. The same AC's field list also omits the new persisted hook products `n_served`, `n_draw`, the CABLE `e0` net load and `power_use_w5`.",
7	   "fix": "Rewrite Method A so reflection over `GraphState` must match the snapshot payload keys exactly, apart from the three holder references. The DERIVED allowlist then applies to the member lists of `GraphCaches`, `GraphScratch` and `GraphDiag`. Add `n_served`, `n_draw`, the CABLE `e0` load and `power_use_w5` to the 'every field the run depends on' list. Add the carry-over note *(Amended 2026-10-29 — ADR-0011 sync)*."
8	  },
9	  {
10	   "where": "LS-17 (L224), the dormancy sentence",
11	   "issue": "The inserted ADR-0012 sentences split the original 'on load M19 also advances ...; then it sets `dormant_since_step` to 0'. The text now reads 'M19 is callable under INIT ..., where it stamps `dormant_since` with the INIT step_no; then it sets `dormant_since_step` to 0'. The natural reading is that the INIT unload stamps the step and immediately zeroes it. That would make the next load's advance `step_no − 0`, so every absolute stamp jumps by the whole session length. The text also names the field both `dormant_since` and `dormant_since_step`.",
12	   "fix": "Move the 'then it sets `dormant_since_step` to 0' clause back to directly follow the load-time advance list. Put the INIT sentence after it as a separate clause. Use `dormant_since_step` throughout."
13	  }
